        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.256,
            0.885,
            0.323
          ],
          "content": "Equally divide the rotis in the situations shown below and write down the share of each child. Are the shares in each of these cases the same? Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.332,
            0.302,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "2 rotis divided equally among 3 children"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.367,
            0.332,
            0.497,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": "4 rotis divided equally among 6 children"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.711,
            0.331,
            0.841,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "6 rotis divided equally among 9 children"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.865,
            0.408,
            0.969,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.553,
            0.851,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": "$\\frac{2}{3}$ is also called the simplest form of $\\frac{4}{6}$ . It is also the simplest form of $\\frac{6}{9}$ as well."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.217,
            0.62,
            0.702,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "Do you notice anything about the relationship between the numerator and denominator in each of these fractions?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.74,
            0.611,
            0.863,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.689,
            0.352,
            0.712
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.717,
            0.475,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "Find the missing numbers:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.741,
            0.814,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "a. glasses of juice shared equally among 4 friends is the same as \\_\\_\\_\\_ glasses of juice shared equally among 8 friends."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.821,
            0.717,
            0.909,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.269,
            0.803,
            0.375,
            0.838
          ],
          "content": "So, ${ \\frac { 5 } { 4 } } = { \\overline { { \\frac { } { 8 } } } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.842,
            0.813,
            0.885
          ],
          "content": "b. 4 kg of potatoes divided equally in 3 bags is the same as 12 kgs of potatoes divided equally in \\_\\_\\_ bags."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.269,
            0.886,
            0.373,
            0.921
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\frac { 4 } { 3 } = \\frac { 1 2 } { \\bigtriangleup }$"
        },
